# Spring Boot / Java 25 — mireserva

Apply these conventions on every change in this project.

## Project structure (current)

```
tdeareserva/
└── mireserva/
    ├── pom.xml                          # Spring Boot 4.x, JPA, WebMVC, PostgreSQL, springdoc
    ├── src/main/java/com/tdea/mireserva/
    │   ├── MireservaApplication.java
    │   ├── controller/                  # REST controllers
    │   ├── entity/                      # JPA entities
    │   ├── repository/                  # Spring Data JPA repositories
    │   ├── service/                     # Business logic
    │   └── dto/                         # Request/Response DTOs (Java records) — create when needed
    ├── src/main/resources/
    │   ├── application.properties
    │   ├── static/
    │   └── templates/
    └── src/test/java/com/tdea/mireserva/
```

Keep layers strict: `controller` → `service` → `repository`. Controllers never talk to repositories directly. Entities never leave the service layer as API payloads — map to/from DTOs.

## Naming (English only)

- Classes, methods, fields, packages, and constants: **English**.
- Use clear domain names (`Reservation`, `findByUserId`, `startDate`).
- Packages: lowercase (`com.tdea.mireserva.service`).
- Classes: PascalCase. Methods/fields: camelCase. Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.

## DTOs = Java records

```java
// ✅ GOOD
public record ReservationRequest(Long roomId, LocalDate startDate, LocalDate endDate) {}

public record ReservationResponse(Long id, String status, LocalDate startDate, LocalDate endDate) {}

// ❌ BAD — mutable DTO classes with getters/setters
```

- Place DTOs under `com.tdea.mireserva.dto`.
- Prefer compact constructors for validation when needed.
- Do not expose JPA entities in controller request/response bodies.

## Javadoc (required on every public method)

Every `public` method must have up-to-date Javadoc: purpose, `@param`, `@return`, and `@throws` when relevant.

```java
/**
 * Creates a new reservation for the given room and date range.
 *
 * @param request reservation data including room and dates
 * @return the persisted reservation as a response DTO
 * @throws IllegalArgumentException if the date range is invalid
 */
public ReservationResponse create(ReservationRequest request) { ... }
```

Update Javadoc whenever signature or behavior changes. Skip redundant Javadoc on trivial `record` accessors.

## Java 25 practices

- Prefer **records** for immutable data (DTOs, value objects).
- Use **pattern matching** for `instanceof` / `switch` when it clarifies branching.
- Prefer **virtual threads** for I/O-bound work (`spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true` when appropriate).
- Prefer **ScopedValue** over `ThreadLocal` for request/tenant/context propagation.
- Use **flexible constructor bodies** to validate before `super(...)` / `this(...)` when useful.
- Prefer `Optional` only as return type for “may be absent”; never as fields or method parameters.
- Prefer `var` only when the type is obvious from the right-hand side; otherwise keep explicit types.
- Avoid preview/incubator APIs in production code.
- Prefer constructor injection; make dependencies `final`. No field injection.
- Prefer immutable collections (`List.of`, `Map.of`) when the collection must not change.

## Spring Boot layering

| Layer | Responsibility | Annotations |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `controller` | HTTP mapping, validation, status codes | `@RestController`, `@RequestMapping` |
| `service` | Business rules, transactions | `@Service`, `@Transactional` |
| `repository` | Persistence only | `JpaRepository` / `@Repository` |
| `entity` | JPA mapping | `@Entity`, `@Table` |
| `dto` | API contracts | `record` |

- Use `@Valid` / Bean Validation on request DTOs.
- Return `ResponseEntity` only when status/headers must vary; otherwise return the DTO and rely on defaults.
- Centralize exception handling with `@RestControllerAdvice`.
- Keep services focused; extract helpers when a class grows beyond a single responsibility.
- Configure via `application.properties` / profiles; never hardcode secrets or environment URLs.

## Persistence

- Entities in `entity/`; repositories in `repository/`.
- Prefer Spring Data derived queries or `@Query` with JPQL; avoid native SQL unless necessary.
- Lazy associations by default; fetch joins only where needed to avoid N+1.
- Do not use bidirectional relationships unless both sides are required.

## Tests

- Place tests under `src/test/java/com/tdea/mireserva/...` mirroring main packages.
- Prefer unit tests for services; slice/integration tests (`@WebMvcTest`, `@DataJpaTest`) when touching HTTP or persistence.
- Name tests in English: `shouldCreateReservationWhenDatesAreValid`.

## Do not

- Spanish identifiers in code.
- Public methods without Javadoc.
- Mutable DTO classes (use records).
- Business logic in controllers or repositories.
- Returning entities from REST endpoints.
- Catch-and-ignore exceptions or empty `catch` blocks.
